    "atom::c86ac1ffe4bd21a78303faa2": {
      "atom_id": "atom::c86ac1ffe4bd21a78303faa2",
      "source_handle": "P0242",
      "field_path": [
        "study_summary_A",
        "problem_or_question"
      ],
      "value": "肠道微生物群促进抗肿瘤免疫的具体分子机制是什么？为何部分患者对PD-1/PD-L1治疗无响应？如何通过靶向微生物相关的免疫检查点通路来克服这种耐药性？",
      "role": "evidence",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::50f6b2c5ac9bd691e19ea9f541284d3dea71a1ff000f8ff332560edd0e0fb6aa",
          "field_path": [
            "study_summary_A",
            "problem_or_question"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "variant_group": "field::569a19d8714ec14f691dc33bf22f7c5dfe116199698b81e62b480bfffeb9e000",
      "multiple_values_in_field": false
    },
    "atom::18a34261580a8ccbe9b80ac9": {
      "atom_id": "atom::18a34261580a8ccbe9b80ac9",
      "source_handle": "P0242",
      "field_path": [
        "study_summary_A",
        "research_scope"
      ],
      "value": "小鼠肿瘤模型（MC38结肠癌、B16黑色素瘤等），涉及无菌鼠（GF）、抗生素处理鼠（ABX）及定植人类/小鼠微生物群的模型；研究对象为肠道微生物群、免疫检查点分子（PD-L2, RGMb）及T细胞功能。",
      "role": "evidence",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::50f6b2c5ac9bd691e19ea9f541284d3dea71a1ff000f8ff332560edd0e0fb6aa",
          "field_path": [
            "study_summary_A",
            "research_scope"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "variant_group": "field::ebd9111293957f782ec09e35e9e81955e415136e930c6a8d5bb5a6b5f1e20c0d",
      "multiple_values_in_field": false
    },
    "atom::02ad5e4a95efd520cc9bf3a4": {
      "atom_id": "atom::02ad5e4a95efd520cc9bf3a4",
      "source_handle": "P0242",
      "field_path": [
        "study_summary_A",
        "work_summary"
      ],
      "value": "本研究旨在揭示肠道微生物群如何调节抗肿瘤免疫反应，特别是针对PD-1/PD-L1抑制剂治疗无响应的情况。研究通过对比不同微生物状态下的免疫反应，发现微生物群通过下调树突状细胞（DCs）上的PD-L2表达来促进抗肿瘤免疫。进一步研究发现，PD-L2不仅结合PD-1，还结合排斥性导向分子b（RGMb）。在缺乏有益菌的模型中，PD-L2和RGMb的高表达抑制了CD8+ T细胞的活性。通过联合阻断PD-L2/RGMb通路或特异性敲除T细胞中的RGMb，可以克服由微生物缺失引起的对PD-1/PD-L1治疗的耐药性。研究还鉴定出特定细菌物种（如Coprobacillus cateniformis）能够诱导这种PD-L2下调，并验证了该机制在人源粪便移植模型中的潜在转化价值。",
      "role": "evidence",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::50f6b2c5ac9bd691e19ea9f541284d3dea71a1ff000f8ff332560edd0e0fb6aa",
          "field_path": [
            "study_summary_A",
            "work_summary"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "variant_group": "field::5ff5e09e2d236a91b71cf9b382281c564ba4f6e2a53eb61649ec5cac7a7018ed",
      "multiple_values_in_field": false
    },
