      "variant_group": "field::b4321fb307cea114c2c31d71617b4418cdb92032aa70cd6f18289400c51a5e5d",
      "multiple_values_in_field": true
    },
    "atom::f5ce6fafc64a7c4165ef38dc": {
      "atom_id": "atom::f5ce6fafc64a7c4165ef38dc",
      "source_handle": "P0269",
      "field_path": [
        "review_planning_B",
        "facet_contributions"
      ],
      "value": {
        "boundaries": "Many mechanisms are derived from murine models or small human subsets. The review notes that the relative contribution of each mechanism in humans is still being elucidated. Some mechanisms (like butyrate's effect) can be context-dependent (positive for anti-PD1, negative for anti-CTLA4).",
        "contribution": "Details proposed mechanisms by which gut microbiota influence ICI efficacy: 1) Production of immunomodulatory metabolites (butyrate, inosine, hippurate); 2) Activation of innate immune receptors (NOD2, STING, TLRs) leading to myeloid cell priming and type I interferon production; 3) Molecular mimicry between bacterial epitopes and tumour neoantigens leading to cross-reactive T cells.",
        "facet_id": "F2"
      },
      "role": "evidence",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::9712641b2fb9f0597c19079bcb14a7662cbc433e4e44b267ee53a4539b2c9aeb",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "facet_contributions",
            "1"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "variant_group": "field::cf93261d72ee0656c7fa52cbc2df875754fc78d8134b308cb1b3c0c1458ab413",
      "multiple_values_in_field": true
    },
    "atom::5ec570da37f0fd8ee743192f": {
      "atom_id": "atom::5ec570da37f0fd8ee743192f",
      "source_handle": "P0269",
      "field_path": [
        "review_planning_B",
        "facet_contributions",
        "possible_uses"
      ],
      "value": "Provides specific mechanistic pathways to explore in the review. These mechanisms explain *how* the microbiome might modulate the immune microenvironment to enhance or suppress ICI response.",
      "role": "planning",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::9712641b2fb9f0597c19079bcb14a7662cbc433e4e44b267ee53a4539b2c9aeb",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "facet_contributions",
            "1",
            "possible_uses"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "variant_group": "field::b4321fb307cea114c2c31d71617b4418cdb92032aa70cd6f18289400c51a5e5d",
      "multiple_values_in_field": true
    },
    "atom::58dccb51dd2cbe24f8feffc9": {
      "atom_id": "atom::58dccb51dd2cbe24f8feffc9",
      "source_handle": "P0269",
      "field_path": [
        "review_planning_B",
        "planning_summary"
      ],
      "value": "This review provides a structured overview of host factors influencing ICI efficacy in solid tumours, with a dedicated section on the gut microbiome. It offers specific mechanistic hypotheses (metabolites, innate immunity, molecular mimicry) and lists candidate microbial taxa associated with response or resistance. This material is useful for contextualizing the role of the host environment in ICI response and for identifying specific mechanistic pathways and microbial species to be investigated in the planned review.",
      "role": "planner_interpretation",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::9712641b2fb9f0597c19079bcb14a7662cbc433e4e44b267ee53a4539b2c9aeb",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "planning_summary"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "variant_group": "field::f05495a914abc8237bd810158a28c71e76b3e1960dbd0a2f5caabb8766275408",
      "multiple_values_in_field": false
    },
    "atom::b043611ba77b73bd423db17a": {
      "atom_id": "atom::b043611ba77b73bd423db17a",
      "source_handle": "P0269",
      "field_path": [
        "review_planning_B",
        "scope_interpretation_cautions"
      ],
      "value": "The review covers multiple cancer types (melanoma, NSCLC, RCC, etc.), so findings should not be assumed to apply uniformly to all solid tumours without checking specific context.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::9712641b2fb9f0597c19079bcb14a7662cbc433e4e44b267ee53a4539b2c9aeb",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "scope_interpretation_cautions",
            "0"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "variant_group": "field::82b318c638ad5e7332776514370a26d4afe6fa0438160483c61b08e20603c6d9",
      "multiple_values_in_field": true
    },
    "atom::ec17513be6040007b4b17183": {
      "atom_id": "atom::ec17513be6040007b4b17183",
      "source_handle": "P0269",
      "field_path": [
        "review_planning_B",
        "scope_interpretation_cautions"
      ],
      "value": "Microbial associations are highly variable; the review explicitly states there is little consensus on specific species, so any single species mentioned should be treated as a candidate rather than a definitive marker.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::9712641b2fb9f0597c19079bcb14a7662cbc433e4e44b267ee53a4539b2c9aeb",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "scope_interpretation_cautions",
            "1"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "variant_group": "field::82b318c638ad5e7332776514370a26d4afe6fa0438160483c61b08e20603c6d9",
      "multiple_values_in_field": true
    },
    "atom::6aa91e78c58f0ef496634db8": {
      "atom_id": "atom::6aa91e78c58f0ef496634db8",
      "source_handle": "P0269",
      "field_path": [
        "review_planning_B",
        "scope_interpretation_cautions"
      ],
      "value": "Mechanisms described are largely hypothetical or based on preclinical models; causal links in humans are not fully established.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "origins": [
        {
