    "atom::e80331c46c052c7581ada8d5": {
      "atom_id": "atom::e80331c46c052c7581ada8d5",
      "source_handle": "P0284",
      "field_path": [
        "review_planning_B",
        "facet_contributions"
      ],
      "value": {
        "boundaries": "The association is observational; causality is inferred through subsequent mechanistic studies but not proven in the clinical cohort alone. Results may vary by cancer type and geography.",
        "contribution": "Validates the clinical association between irAEs and improved ICI outcomes across multiple solid tumor cohorts (melanoma and NSCLC), confirming that higher-grade irAEs correlate with longer OS and PFS. Identifies specific microbial signatures (e.g., S. vestibularis, H. porci) associated with both irAE and response states.",
        "facet_id": "F1"
      },
      "role": "evidence",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::c66fbeaa280c108e014af7cc09f0b2e5689f094a55d8a7f2b398b693ae815e7a",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "facet_contributions",
            "0"
          ]
        },
        {
          "record_id": "record::384337303cf1d585cd3ac32afaeb624f5aebb4f4c45b3d47c5eee039228c9cc0",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "facet_contributions",
            "0"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "variant_group": "field::59d7199f614ab4ef5f13ca49b4668fad8566b77ed5bbaa73f9e1f2e9fa6c0fd3",
      "multiple_values_in_field": true
    },
    "atom::cf7d7cf5a9b18e2b689215e2": {
      "atom_id": "atom::cf7d7cf5a9b18e2b689215e2",
      "source_handle": "P0284",
      "field_path": [
        "review_planning_B",
        "facet_contributions",
        "possible_uses"
      ],
      "value": "Can be used to support the general observation that microbiome composition correlates with ICI efficacy and toxicity. Provides data on how irAE status serves as a proxy for favorable microbial environments in some contexts.",
      "role": "planning",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::c66fbeaa280c108e014af7cc09f0b2e5689f094a55d8a7f2b398b693ae815e7a",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "facet_contributions",
            "0",
            "possible_uses"
          ]
        },
        {
          "record_id": "record::384337303cf1d585cd3ac32afaeb624f5aebb4f4c45b3d47c5eee039228c9cc0",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "facet_contributions",
            "0",
            "possible_uses"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "variant_group": "field::3c2854869723d8d678db64859c62a9b8087614bf48255003021bd5247e9ae4a9",
      "multiple_values_in_field": true
    },
    "atom::f5b77f6f89c89b517fbf6126": {
      "atom_id": "atom::f5b77f6f89c89b517fbf6126",
      "source_handle": "P0284",
      "field_path": [
        "review_planning_B",
        "facet_contributions"
      ],
      "value": {
        "boundaries": "The mechanism is derived from mouse models and in vitro assays; the exact metabolite identity is unknown. The effect of live bacteria on barrier integrity is distinct from the metabolite's effect on tumor response, highlighting complex, context-dependent interactions.",
        "contribution": "Demonstrates a specific mechanism where Paraclostridium bifermentans enhances ICI efficacy via a secreted low-molecular-weight metabolite (< 3 kDa), while simultaneously causing ir-colitis through live-bacteria-induced epithelial barrier disruption. Shows that FMT from ir-colitis patients transfers both inflammatory potential and enhanced ICI response.",
        "facet_id": "F2"
      },
      "role": "evidence",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::c66fbeaa280c108e014af7cc09f0b2e5689f094a55d8a7f2b398b693ae815e7a",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "facet_contributions",
            "1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "record_id": "record::384337303cf1d585cd3ac32afaeb624f5aebb4f4c45b3d47c5eee039228c9cc0",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "facet_contributions",
            "1"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "variant_group": "field::59d7199f614ab4ef5f13ca49b4668fad8566b77ed5bbaa73f9e1f2e9fa6c0fd3",
      "multiple_values_in_field": true
    },
    "atom::fdd7b314e0a9087e58a13b81": {
      "atom_id": "atom::fdd7b314e0a9087e58a13b81",
      "source_handle": "P0284",
      "field_path": [
        "review_planning_B",
        "facet_contributions",
        "possible_uses"
      ],
      "value": "Provides a detailed mechanistic example of how a single microbe can have dual, distinct effects on host physiology (toxicity vs. efficacy). Illustrates the role of microbial metabolites in potentiating ICI, offering a potential avenue for targeted therapies (e.g., purified metabolites).",
      "role": "planning",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::c66fbeaa280c108e014af7cc09f0b2e5689f094a55d8a7f2b398b693ae815e7a",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "facet_contributions",
            "1",
            "possible_uses"
          ]
        },
        {
          "record_id": "record::384337303cf1d585cd3ac32afaeb624f5aebb4f4c45b3d47c5eee039228c9cc0",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "facet_contributions",
            "1",
            "possible_uses"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "variant_group": "field::3c2854869723d8d678db64859c62a9b8087614bf48255003021bd5247e9ae4a9",
      "multiple_values_in_field": true
    },
    "atom::ffd393a9dc25e87f69172e96": {
      "atom_id": "atom::ffd393a9dc25e87f69172e96",
      "source_handle": "P0284",
      "field_path": [
        "review_planning_B",
        "planning_summary"
      ],
      "value": "This paper offers concrete mechanistic insights into how the gut microbiome modulates ICI efficacy, specifically addressing the 'dual role' of certain bacteria in causing toxicity while boosting anti-tumor immunity. It provides a rare example of a single bacterial species (Paraclostridium bifermentans) being functionally linked to both irAE and efficacy, distinguishing between live-bacteria-dependent inflammatory effects and metabolite-mediated immunostimulatory effects. This is valuable for explaining mechanisms where microbial components directly influence host physiology and immune response.",
      "role": "planner_interpretation",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::c66fbeaa280c108e014af7cc09f0b2e5689f094a55d8a7f2b398b693ae815e7a",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "planning_summary"
          ]
        },
        {
          "record_id": "record::384337303cf1d585cd3ac32afaeb624f5aebb4f4c45b3d47c5eee039228c9cc0",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "planning_summary"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "variant_group": "field::3fb060a6caed34ba216820ae34afe20eb6c6c990d796e11d98d39b4eae1cfc14",
      "multiple_values_in_field": false
    },
    "atom::9964b8d843b952c18995daf5": {
      "atom_id": "atom::9964b8d843b952c18995daf5",
      "source_handle": "P0284",
      "field_path": [
        "review_planning_B",
        "scope_interpretation_cautions"
      ],
      "value": "The study identifies P. bifermentans as a key player, but the exact metabolite responsible for the anti-tumor effect is not characterized; do not overstate the specificity of the molecular mechanism.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::c66fbeaa280c108e014af7cc09f0b2e5689f094a55d8a7f2b398b693ae815e7a",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "scope_interpretation_cautions",
            "0"
          ]
        },
        {
          "record_id": "record::384337303cf1d585cd3ac32afaeb624f5aebb4f4c45b3d47c5eee039228c9cc0",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "scope_interpretation_cautions",
            "0"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "variant_group": "field::ffe0ceb3c10e87298b47fe260a4fee8638489cab16b2aa112785c225e8355c16",
      "multiple_values_in_field": true
    },
    "atom::1482d971688f8c6a45f4eb09": {
      "atom_id": "atom::1482d971688f8c6a45f4eb09",
      "source_handle": "P0284",
      "field_path": [
        "review_planning_B",
        "scope_interpretation_cautions"
      ],
      "value": "Mouse models used (MCA-205, DSS) have limitations in fully recapitulating human ir-colitis; results should be framed as preclinical evidence supporting human observations.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::c66fbeaa280c108e014af7cc09f0b2e5689f094a55d8a7f2b398b693ae815e7a",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "scope_interpretation_cautions",
            "1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "record_id": "record::384337303cf1d585cd3ac32afaeb624f5aebb4f4c45b3d47c5eee039228c9cc0",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "scope_interpretation_cautions",
            "1"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "variant_group": "field::ffe0ceb3c10e87298b47fe260a4fee8638489cab16b2aa112785c225e8355c16",
      "multiple_values_in_field": true
    },
    "atom::c16c42850044684ec971f685": {
      "atom_id": "atom::c16c42850044684ec971f685",
      "source_handle": "P0284",
      "field_path": [
        "review_planning_B",
        "scope_interpretation_cautions"
      ],
      "value": "The 'dual role' of P. bifermentans involves two different mechanisms (live bacteria for toxicity, metabolite for efficacy); ensure this distinction is clear when citing.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::c66fbeaa280c108e014af7cc09f0b2e5689f094a55d8a7f2b398b693ae815e7a",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "scope_interpretation_cautions",
            "2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "record_id": "record::384337303cf1d585cd3ac32afaeb624f5aebb4f4c45b3d47c5eee039228c9cc0",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "scope_interpretation_cautions",
            "2"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "variant_group": "field::ffe0ceb3c10e87298b47fe260a4fee8638489cab16b2aa112785c225e8355c16",
      "multiple_values_in_field": true
    },
    "atom::cafb8802dcc1f5812d97e5ec": {
      "atom_id": "atom::cafb8802dcc1f5812d97e5ec",
      "source_handle": "P0284",
      "field_path": [
        "review_planning_B",
        "scope_interpretation_cautions"
      ],
      "value": "Clinical associations are based on retrospective/prospective cohorts with potential confounders; causality is established primarily through animal models, not clinical intervention.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::c66fbeaa280c108e014af7cc09f0b2e5689f094a55d8a7f2b398b693ae815e7a",
